"opening": "We are refining the performance and flexibility of core utility functions in more-itertools. These changes enhance existing behaviors by optimizing internal deduplication strategies and extending comparison capabilities with key-based transformations.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m01",
"text": "The `totient` function must compute Euler's totient using `set()` for deduplication to ensure correct results with improved performance."
},
{
"id": "m02",
"text": "The `all_equal` function must accept an optional `key` parameter that allows callers to transform items before performing the equality check."
},
{
"id": "m03",
"text": "When a `key` is provided, `all_equal` must compare items after applying the key function, returning True only if all transformed values are equal."
